thub.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-27T15:21:03Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T15:21:03Z","body":"> The code looks fine, but I wonder about usefulness of this change 🤔 It can potentially prevent errors, but not sure when it's relevant if it doesn't fix the previously linked issue.\r\n\r\nThe PR and this issue: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109496 should be closed, Those changes are part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109396 and the issue itself was fixed here https://github.com/TokisanGames/Terrain3D/pull/779\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3228654935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3228677603","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3228677603","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3228677603,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AcbXj","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-27T15:27:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T15:27:09Z","body":"I wonder if we can at least make the error more clear? The problem was fixed only after the discussion, but it's not documented anywhere outside the issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3228677603/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3242142169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3242142169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3242142169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BPynZ","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-01T12:16:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T00:42:13Z","body":"> I wonder if we can at least make the error more clear? The problem was fixed only after the discussion, but it's not documented anywhere outside the issue.\r\n\r\nI have no issue with calling `EditorInterface.edit_node()` many times or showing/hiding the plugin button many times in the same frame on Linux, but I have found an issue, calling `edit_node()` in the same frame where `EditorPlugin._handles()` calls `EditorPlugin._edit()` results in thousands of errors.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"961\" height=\"391\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b897966-bbc9-42fd-8784-ff50b3be1ae5\" />\r\n\r\nAnd waiting one frame before calling `edit_node()` makes `_edit()` called one extra time with `<Object#null>`, please check if this can trigger the same issue on Windows.\r\n\r\nDouble click any SVG file to trigger `_edit()` ie. `icon.svg`.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends EditorPlugin\r\n\r\nvar panel: PanelContainer\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _enable_plugin() -> void:\r\n\tpanel = PanelContainer.new()\r\n\tadd_control_to_bottom_panel(panel, \"Bottom Panel Test\")\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _disable_plugin() -> void:\r\n\tremove_control_from_bottom_panel(panel)\r\n\tpanel.free()\r\n\tpanel = null\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _edit(object: Object) -> void:\r\n\tprint(object)\r\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\r\n\tEditorInterface.edit_node(get_tree().edited_scene_root)\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _handles(object: Object) -> bool:\r\n\tvar res: Resource = object as Resource\r\n\tif not res:\r\n\t\treturn false\r\n\treturn res.resource_path.ends_with(\"svg\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nEach `_edit()` call prints.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<CompressedTexture2D#-9223366879286766564>\r\n<Object#null>\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3242142169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309403531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309403531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309403531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FQX2L","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T19:49:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T19:49:03Z","body":"I did check it and I indeed get double print. Without `await` the editor will crash from what looks like stack overflow.\r\n\r\nAlthough this behavior is expected. `edit_node()` does call `_handles()` in the plugin, and then `edit(null)`, because another plugin is going to edit the object.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309403531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309465663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309465663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309465663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FQnA_","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T20:02:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T20:06:20Z","body":"> Although this behavior is expected. `edit_node()` does call `_handles()` in the plugin, and then `edit(null)`, because another plugin is going to edit the object.\r\n\r\nSounds like a bug or unexpected behavior, we can discuss it later since the docs here says that `_edit()` will be called later with `null` Object to allow cleaning the plugin, which makes `edit_node()` tells the same plugin that just handled the `Object` and returned `true` to clean, it's confusing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309465663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309486652","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309486652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309486652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FQsI8","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T20:06:41Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T20:06:41Z","body":"Well, only one object can be edited by any plugin at the time (it's actually one per \"context\", but in this case the SVG file and scene root share the context). Hence if you try to edit another object, the current plugin, which does not handle it, has to cleanup.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309486652/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309503587","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309503587","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309503587,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FQwRj","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T20:09:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T20:15:43Z","body":"Yes but we have an exception here when `_handles(Object)` returns `true` it already calls `_edit(Object)` and `_edit(null)` at same frame which is indeed a bug. We should exclude the Plugins that can handle the `Object` from the cleanup.\r\n\r\nEdit: This also can be fixed if the clean up happens before the handling which should be the expected behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309503587/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309539944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309539944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309539944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FQ5Jo","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T20:17:15Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T20:17:15Z","body":"`edit_node()` requests editor to edit the node. The editor goes through all relevant plugins, calls `_handles()` passing the object and if a plugin returns `true` for the object, the editor will call `_edit()`.\r\n\r\nWhat happens in your code:\r\n- You click SVG file\r\n- Editor gets edit request from FileSystem dock\r\n- Your plugin receives `_handles()` call and returns true\r\n- Your plugin receives `_edit()` call\r\n- In the `_edit()` callback, you request to edit _another_ object\r\n- The editor gets request and goes over plugins\r\n- Your plugin gets a `_handles()` call with the new object that you just requested and returns `false`\r\n- _Another_ plugin returns true for `_handles()`\r\n- Your plugin receives `_edit(null)`, because it no longer edits (doesn't matter if it was editing a different object)\r\n- Another plugin receives `_edit(the new object)` call","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309539944/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3309608537","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109502#issuecomment-3309608537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109502","id":3309608537,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FRJ5Z","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","ty